// GPU class: medium
//
// States a texture edge of 2048 voxels and 8 GB of texture memory. 2048 is the
// hard limit that every known WebGL device holds, so `medium` and `high`
// differ only by memory.
//
// `medium` is the OHIF default, so this file states in the URL what the viewer
// already does. Load it to return to the default after another profile. A
// device of the middle class crashed with more texture memory than 8 GB.
//
// The profile is a stated value and not a measurement. Nothing probes the
// device, so a real device may hold more or less than this profile states.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/medium`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuCapabilityProfile": "medium"
  }
}
